IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 4, section 11A (pass 2).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Pass 1 left s 11A inert as "how the compilation is laid out". It says where an inserted definition
-- or list item goes, which decides what a person reading the amended Act finds at each place, so it is encoded: a function from the
-- existing items and the new one to the position the new one takes. "Letter-by-letter" means the letters only: the key of an item is
-- its lower-case letters with spaces and hyphens taken out. Where the amending Act specifies the position, where the list was not
-- arranged alphabetically, or where the new item has the same letters as an existing one, the section does not say: NOTHING.

§ `Part 4: Amendment, repeal and expiry of Acts (section 11A)`

§§ `Section 11A: inserting definitions into provisions or inserting items into lists or tables`

GIVEN item IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the letter-by-letter key of` item MEANS
    REPLACE (REPLACE (TOLOWER item) " " "") "-" ""

GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the keys are in order` keys MEANS
    CONSIDER keys
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER rest
        WHEN second FOLLOWED BY more THEN first AT MOST second AND `the keys are in order` rest
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN items IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the items are arranged alphabetically, letter by letter` items MEANS
    `the keys are in order` (map `the letter-by-letter key of` items)

GIVEN items IS A LIST OF STRING
      addition IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the position among the items, counting from 0, where the new item goes` items addition MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN i YIELD `the letter-by-letter key of` i EQUALS `the letter-by-letter key of` addition) items
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (count (filter (GIVEN i YIELD `the letter-by-letter key of` i LESS THAN `the letter-by-letter key of` addition) items))

-- src:294 | (1) If an amending Act inserts a definition in a provision of the Act being amended, but does not specify the position in that provision where it is to be inserted, it is to be inserted in the appropriate alphabetical position, determined on a letter-by-letter basis.
-- src:295 | Inserting items into lists or tables
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 11A(1) (src:294-295)
GIVEN `the amending Act specifies the position` IS A BOOLEAN
      definitions IS A LIST OF STRING
      addition IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the position of the inserted definition among the definitions, counting from 0` `the amending Act specifies the position` definitions addition MEANS
    IF `the amending Act specifies the position`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `the position among the items, counting from 0, where the new item goes` definitions addition

-- src:296 | (2) If:
-- src:297 | (a) an amending Act inserts an item into a list or table in a provision of the Act being amended, but does not specify the position in the list or table where the item is to be inserted; and
-- src:298 | (b) immediately before the insertion, the list or table was arranged alphabetically;
-- src:299 | the item is inserted in the appropriate alphabetical position, determined on a letter-by-letter basis.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 11A(2) (src:296-299)
GIVEN `the amending Act specifies the position` IS A BOOLEAN
      items IS A LIST OF STRING
      addition IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the position of the inserted item among the items, counting from 0` `the amending Act specifies the position` items addition MEANS
    IF `the amending Act specifies the position` OR (NOT `the items are arranged alphabetically, letter by letter` items)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `the position among the items, counting from 0, where the new item goes` items addition
